-- title:
--   Base change to ℚ̄ of the two Igusa chart algebras
-- statement:
--   Let $N$ be a natural number with $N \neq 0$ and let $\ell$ be a natural number (no primality of $\ell$ is required). Write $\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}$ for [`GaloisRep.ratLocalizedAt ℓ`](def/GaloisRep_Flat.html#L8), the subring of $\mathbb{Q}$ consisting of those rationals whose denominator is coprime to $\ell$, and $F =$ `modularFunctionFieldFull N`, the subfield of the Laurent series field over $\mathbb{Q}$ generated by `divisorExpansions N`. Let `chartAlgFin N ℓ` and `chartAlgInf N ℓ` be the $\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}$-subalgebras `chartAlg N ℓ` of $F$ attached to the singletons $\{j\}$ and $\{j^{-1}\}$, where $j =$ `jFull N` is the $q$-expansion of $j$. On the other side, `modularFunctionFieldBar N` is the base change of $F$ to $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ inside the Laurent series field over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, $\bar j =$ `jBar N` is the coefficientwise image of $j$ there, and for a subset $S$, [`AlgebraicCurve.CurveModel.chartRing`](def/JacJ1_ChartAlgebra.html#L45) $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}\,S$ denotes the $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-subalgebra of elements integral over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}[S]$. The assertion is the conjunction of two existence statements: there is an isomorphism of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-algebras $e_{\mathrm{Fin}} \colon \overline{\mathbb{Q}} \otimes_{\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}}$ `chartAlgFin N ℓ` $\xrightarrow{\sim}$ `chartRing` $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}\,\{\bar j\}$ carrying, for every $b$ in `chartAlgFin N ℓ`, the pure tensor $1 \otimes b$ to the element of `modularFunctionFieldBar N` obtained by applying `coeffEmb` (coefficientwise application of $\mathbb{Q} \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$) to the Laurent series $b$; and likewise an isomorphism $e_{\mathrm{Inf}} \colon \overline{\mathbb{Q}} \otimes_{\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}}$ `chartAlgInf N ℓ` $\xrightarrow{\sim}$ `chartRing` $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}\,\{\bar j^{-1}\}$ with the same compatibility on pure tensors.
--
--   This identifies the generic fibre of each of the two affine charts of the Igusa scheme [`ModularCurve.IgusaScheme`](def/ModularCurve_IgusaScheme.html#L255) with the corresponding $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-chart ring of the modular function field, the compatibility clause pinning the isomorphisms down by coefficientwise extension of scalars on $q$-expansions. It is used throughout the comparison of the integral model with the $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-curve model, in particular by the lemmas on closed points, crossings and reductions in the Deligne–Rapoport model package.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_IgusaScheme_exists_algEquiv_tensor_chartAlg_chartRing.lean

